\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Experiment 1: Multi-Detector Comparison on Synthetic Drift Patterns. MTD = Mean Time to Detection (samples); MDR = Missed Detection Rate; FA = False Alarms. ``---'' indicates the detector missed all drift points.}}{51}{table.caption.95}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Experiment 2: EADD vs.\ D3 on the four annotated real-world datasets. Prec.\ = Precision; Rec.\ = Recall on known drift points; MTD = Mean Time to Detection (samples; lower is better). Bold indicates EADD outperforms D3. ``---'' = all known drift points missed. Low precision on incremental datasets reflects the INSECTS annotation convention: only major transition boundaries are annotated; additional detections may correspond to unannotated continuous incremental changes rather than false alarms. Data from \texttt {experiment2\_realworld.csv}.}}{56}{table.caption.103}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Supplementary Multi-Detector Comparison on 11-stream subset with annotated datasets. MTD = Mean Time to Detection (samples). ``---'' = detector missed all annotated drifts or timed out.}}{57}{table.caption.104}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Experiment 2: Detection counts on nine unannotated real-world datasets (EADD vs.\ D3). Ground-truth drift counts are unknown; counts indicate detection activity, not false alarm rates. Data from \texttt {experiment2\_realworld.csv}.}}{57}{table.caption.105}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Experiment 3: SHAP Feature Attribution Accuracy. P@k = Precision at $k$ (fraction of top-$k$ features that are truly drifted); R@k = Recall at $k$ (fraction of drifted features in top-$k$); F1@k = harmonic mean. DSI = AUC $\times $ (1 $-$ $H_{\text {norm}}(\mathbf {s})$); higher DSI indicates more concentrated, severe drift. All DSI values fall in the Low tier ($< 0.3$). In the Prescription column, $\text {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "558$}$ indicates that the automated SHAP-based drift-type classification correctly matched the ground-truth drift scenario.}}{63}{table.caption.118}%
